CONTAINMENT SWEEP COMPLETED around this bead, so the class is closed and the nulls are on record rather than being re-measured by the next lane.

EDGE LABELS -- CLEAN. A 62-character edge label renders ELLIPSIZED ("...that wil<ellipsis>") inside a box sized to the truncated text (rect w=328, text anchor=middle centred in it). So "labels get fitted to their box" is already this engine's policy elsewhere, which is what makes option (a) on this bead consistent rather than novel.

SEQUENCE -- CLEAN, all four sub-surfaces measured on a 49-character participant name:
  participant box grows with the name (w=449.85 for the long one vs 100 for "B"), label centred in it;
  lifeline SPACING grows with box width (lifelines at 235.46 and 700.11, a 465px gap), so the lifeline-side label has room -- checked for collision at per-char ratios 0.45 and 0.50 and it is clear at both;
  activation bar is centred on its lifeline (bar 694.85..704.85 against a lifeline centred 699.85);
  message-label boxes are sized to their text (w=43 for "go", 58 for "done", text centred).

So of the three surfaces I listed as unswept on bd-tm5p, two are clean and this one is the hit. Hit rate has dropped, so I am stopping the sweep rather than manufacturing more probes.

WORTH NOTING FOR WHOEVER FIXES THIS: the sequence result is the design this bead's option (b) would copy -- participant boxes size to their text and the LIFELINE SPACING absorbs it, so nothing overflows and nothing is truncated. A gantt task-name column would work the same way. That is an argument that (b) is the coherent choice for this engine, not just the mermaid-compatible one. Still not my call to make unilaterally.
